# Third-party notices

This project is MIT-licensed (see `LICENSE`). It vendors two browser libraries so the
dashboard needs no build chain; both keep their own license notices inside the vendored
file, and their exact upstream version and file hashes are recorded next to the file.

| Package | Version | License | Upstream | Vendored at |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Alpine.js | see `PROVENANCE.json` | MIT | https://github.com/alpinejs/alpine | `src/web/public/assets/vendor/alpinejs/` |
| uPlot | see `PROVENANCE.json` | MIT | https://github.com/leeoniya/uPlot | `src/web/public/assets/vendor/uplot/` |

Notes:

- Versions are not duplicated here on purpose - `PROVENANCE.json` in each vendor
  directory is the single source, and `pnpm run vendor:check` verifies the files still
  match it (`test/unit/vendor.test.ts`).
- Neither vendored file may be hand-edited: `pnpm run vendor` re-syncs from the pinned
  upstream version.

OpenTTD itself is not distributed with this repository and is licensed separately
(GPLv2); the harness drives the user's own OpenTTD binary through the Admin Port.
